# ser2netweb — the minimum dependencies: every floor of pyproject.toml, exactly, and for the
# packages these need in turn the oldest release a distribution in docs/PACKAGING.md
# ships (that they accept). CI's job "minimum dependencies" installs this file alone
# (pip install --no-deps, then pip check) on Python 3.10, the oldest supported, and runs
# the whole suite on it. It is a test of the floors, not a way to install ser2netweb:
# requirements.txt and requirements-lock.txt are the tested, shipped set. (Not named
# *.txt, so that Dependabot, which updates requirements files, leaves these versions be.)
#
# pyserial-asyncio-fast is left out on purpose: its floor is its pin (0.16), which every
# other job runs with, and most distributions don't package it, so this job runs on
# ser2netweb's copy of its transport (ser2netweb/engine/serial_transport.py), as they do.
# tests/test_pyproject.py checks this file against pyproject.toml.
